Armor All was new, and White says cleaning wheels and treating tires could make a car look brand new. The doorman and White saw that they could work on the car while the customer was already occupied. The offer was not complicated: $P_{\mathrm{detail}}=\text{\$20}.$ That is the only price the transcript gives. We should not infer margins, costs, volume, or profitability. The evidence supports a narrower and stronger mechanism: $\begin{aligned}
\text{parked car}+\text{dinner window}
&\longrightarrow \text{service interval},\\
\text{service interval}+\text{visible improvement}
&\longrightarrow \text{simple offer},\\
\text{simple offer}+\text{delivered result}
&\longrightarrow \text{first business}.\end{aligned}$

