p.src:
The example is deliberately ordinary. A founder has a strong week, does a few thousand dollars of business, and suddenly feels permitted to buy a suit at Saks Fifth Avenue or a $\$200$ bottle of wine. The relation is: $\text{business win}
\longrightarrow
\text{personal spending temptation}.$ This is not accounting. It is behavioral mechanics. The danger is that a revenue event gets mistaken for durable wealth.

