Because the total overhaul creates too many failure points at once. White describes the familiar resolution pattern: stop A, B, C, D and start E, F, G, H. The person reaches A and B, fails, feels ashamed, turns on Netflix, gets chips, and begins again from disappointment. The smaller loop is: $\text{choose one action}
\longrightarrow
\text{complete it}
\longrightarrow
\text{reflect}
\longrightarrow
\text{repeat}.$

