p.src:
The final diagnostic step is the Achilles heel. White lists examples such as sugar, vodka, marijuana, a bad marriage, or being mean to people. The useful action is therefore not just any small action: $\text{Useful Action}
=
\text{Small Enough to Complete}
+
\text{Close to the Real Constraint}.$ This ties founder discipline back to business judgment. A company improves when the owner stops hiding the constraint, names it accurately, and chooses the next action small enough to be done.

